// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
// A/B COST MODEL (pinned in code, NOT left to the Properties tab). Commission and
// slippage default to ZERO in TradingView, and zero costs systematically FLATTER the
// Treatment arm specifically: it is designed to fire materially more trades, so it pays
// more spread, and a costless test hides exactly the degradation the acceptance criteria
// are meant to measure. Pinning them here also removes the risk of the two arms being
// run under different Properties settings, which would invalidate the comparison
// outright. slippage is in TICKS; commission is cash per contract per side. TUNE BOTH
// to your own broker's XAUUSD fill quality before trusting absolute P&L — but keep them
// IDENTICAL across the two arms, which is what actually matters for a gate-only A/B.
//
// CHANGE ID: P0-CAL-002 — SELF-CORRECTION of the values pinned in the previous pass, and
// reconciliation of the TWO cost models that were silently disagreeing.
//   (1) UNIT ERROR (mine): strategy()'s `slippage` is denominated in TICKS, while the
//       Master's internal analog-cost model uses slippagePts in POINTS. `slippage=2` was
//       therefore 0.02 points/side at a 0.01 mintick — 10x too small (100x at 0.001) —
//       against the 0.2 points/side the expectancy engine assumes. Now 20 ticks = 0.20
//       points/side at mintick 0.01, matching slippagePts exactly.
//   (2) COMMISSION DIVERGENCE: commissionL defaulted to 0.0, so the Master's EV/veto
//       priced commission at ZERO while the backtest charged it. Both now assume the
//       same ~$7/lot round turn (commissionL=7.0; 3.50 per contract per SIDE here).
// WHY THIS MATTERS beyond tidiness: the Master's cost model feeds _costATR, which feeds
// analog expectancy, which drives the negative-expectancy VETO. Mispricing cost there
// means the system SELECTS trades under one cost assumption and is SCORED under another
// — an A/B measured on that basis is not measuring the gates. Selector and scorer must
// agree.
//
// CHANGE ID: P0-CAL-004 — values above DERIVED, not guessed, and proven equal by the
// cost-equivalence harness (cost_invariant.py). Two further faults this exposed:
//
//   (A) QTY UNIT ERROR (100x). strategy() qty is in UNITS OF THE BASE INSTRUMENT; for
//       spot XAUUSD the base is XAU = ONE TROY OUNCE, so qty=1 is 1 oz, NOT one 100oz
//       lot. commission_value=3.50 "per contract" therefore charged $3.50 per OUNCE per
//       side = $700 round turn per lot — 100x the intended $7/lot. Since pointValue=100
//       encodes 100 oz/lot, the correct figure is 7.00/100/2 = 0.035 per contract PER SIDE.
//
//   (B) THE ENGINE HAS NO SPREAD PARAMETER. The selector charges _sessSpread; the scorer
//       charged nothing for it. Spread is therefore FOLDED INTO slippage here. With the
//       spreadCost input at its 0.3 default, _sessSpread = max(floor, 0.3) collapses to
//       0.30 for killzone/NY/London alike, so one constant matches every in-session bar
//       exactly: (0.30 spread + 0.40 slip round trip) / 2 / 0.01 = 35 ticks.
//
// DERIVATION — recompute these if you change ANY of spreadCost, slippagePts, commissionL,
// pointValue or mintick, or the two models silently desynchronise again:
//   commission_value = commissionL / (pointValue) / 2
//   slippage_ticks   = (spreadCost + 2*slippagePts) / 2 / syminfo.mintick
//
// KNOWN RESIDUAL (accepted, documented): off-session bars carry a 0.50 spread floor in
// the selector vs the 0.30 folded in here — the scorer under-charges them by 0.20 points.
// strategy() takes ONE constant, so no single value can match a session-varying spread.
// The sessionQuality >= 30 hard gate excludes off-session bars in practice, so this
// residual should affect no trade the A/B actually takes; if you lower that gate, revisit.
//
// These are BROKER-SPECIFIC, not universal truths. $7/lot round turn and 0.2 pts/side are
// mid-range retail ECN gold figures. Replace with your own fills, rerun the derivation
// above, and keep BOTH arms identical.
strategy("XAUUSD Quantum 5.0 — Control", overlay=true, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=500, max_boxes_count=500, max_bars_back=5000, initial_capital=10000, default_qty_type=strategy.fixed, default_qty_value=1, calc_on_every_tick=false, process_orders_on_close=true, commission_type=strategy.commission.cash_per_contract, commission_value=0.035, slippage=35)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// FILE ROLE: A/B CONTROL ARM — DEPRECATED GATES, BACKTEST ONLY. DO NOT DEPLOY.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// XAUUSD Quantum 4.0 — Post-Audit Remediation
string QVERSION = "Q7.2"
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Master notes follow:
// dashboard — the file to trade from. Two strategy TWINS exist for backtesting
// only (Strategy = current gates, Strategy_OLDGATES = pre-Q5.5 control); neither
// is a deployment target. See each twin's header.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ═══ Q5.4-CORE: chart-drawing layer (runVisuals + plot/fill/bgcolor statements)
// removed to satisfy the 100,256 compiled-token limit (build was at 128,210).
// ALL analytical engines, the dashboard, trade plan, and alerts are intact — the
// dashboard and plan panel remain the primary interface. Chart visuals (FVG/OB boxes,
// BOS/CHoCH labels, forecast cone, key-level lines, session shading, EMA/VWAP/BB
// overlays) can be provided as a separate lightweight companion script on request. ═══ // Version: Quantum 5.0 MASTER — R6.0 + quant-audit statistical-integrity pass
// ═══════════════ Q5.4-AuctionIQ — interpretive auction layer (final AMT spec) ═══════════════
//  B1  Directional states: ACCEPT -> ACC-HI/ACC-LO; REJECTION -> REJ-HI/REJ-LO.
//  B2  7-stage cycle: BAL > INIT > DISC > TEST > ACPT > TRND > EXH.
//  B3  Acceptance grade (A+/A/B/C/D); rejection tier (WEAK/MOD/STRONG/INST).
//  B4  Discovery tiers: FAILED / DEVELOPING / CONFIRMED / ACCEPTED / EXHAUSTED.
//  B5  Opening types + GAP-DRV / GAP-FILL / O-NEU / DLY-DRV.
//  B6  Value migration 5-tier (strong/developing higher-lower/balanced).
//  B7  Market Personality (day type): TREND / NORM-VAR / NORMAL / NEUTRAL / BAL day,
//      from day-direction ratio and EWMA average day range.
//  B8  Initiative activity (INIT-BUY/SELL, RESP-BUY/SELL, BALANCED), Inventory
//      (VWAP-deviation in ATR), Rotation quality (HLTH/POOR/XTRM/FAIL).
//  B9  Auction narrative: last four DISTINCT states as a one-line chain.
//  B10 Auction bias replaces raw signal wording in the auction line:
//      LONG/SHORT-CONT vs LONG/SHORT-REV vs NO TRADE/WAIT.
//  Approximations stated: double-distribution day detection is not implementable
//  without intraday profile splits (excluded, same O(n) rationale as TPO).
// ═══════════════ Q5.3-Auction — Institutional Auction Intelligence layer ═══════════════
// IMPLEMENTED (all O(1), non-repainting, built on validated engines):
//  A1  AUCTION STATE ENGINE — 8 states (BALANCE / TREND AUCTION / ROTATIONAL /
//      DISCOVERY / ACCEPTANCE / REJECTION / EXHAUSTION / ACCUM-DIST) scored from
//      existing composites; ONE dominant state with a normalized probability.
//  A2  AUCTION CYCLE — Balance>Search>Test>Acceptance>Expansion>Exhaustion stage,
//      derived from state + regime, with progress glyph.
//  A3  ACCEPTANCE ENGINE — 0-100 from time-on-side of value, close location, relative
//      volume, and ATR-normalized follow-through.
//  A4  VALUE MIGRATION — daily VWAP as the value proxy (labeled approximation);
//      yesterday-vs-today value with direction interpretation.
//  A5  PRICE DISCOVERY — Strong/Moderate/Weak/Rotational from value distance, ATR
//      percentile, ADX, acceptance, structure persistence.
//  A6  OPENING TYPE — Open Drive / Open Test Drive / Open Rejection Reverse /
//      Open Auction, classified from the live session's excursion geometry.
//  A7  LIQUIDITY SWEEP QUALITY — every sweep graded 0-100 (A-D) from penetration,
//      volume percentile, reversal efficiency, displacement.
//  A8  VIX feed (na-guarded, ignore_invalid_symbol) as a risk-state display.
// DEFERRED — with Pine-limit / validation rationale:
//  - True per-bar historical Market Profile (IB, single prints, HVN/LVN maps): requires
//    nested loops over history per bar — violates the O(n) budget; the live-edge VP
//    (POC/VAH/VAL) remains the honest approximation and already feeds the plan.
//  - FVG fill-probability / OB failure-probability NUMBERS: no validated estimator is
//    available in-script; publishing invented percentages would violate the scientific-
//    validation rule. Age/quality/mitigation states remain; probabilities stay with the
//    analog engine, which is calibrated.
//  - "Bayesian" posterior: the aggregation remains honest adaptive evidence weighting +
//    Platt-fitted probability (a true prior/likelihood decomposition is not estimable
//    from OHLCV within Pine; renaming weighting as Bayes would be mislabeling).
//  - Full dashboard re-layout: all specified fields exist; regrouping ~60 cells is
//    cosmetic and untestable headlessly — auction fields are integrated into the
//    MARKET/session cell instead.
// ═══════════════ Q5.2-AutoForecast ═══════════════
//  F1  Analog gating reworked: HARD gate on STATE similarity alone (+ optional
//      minMatchQ floor); recency decay is now a floor cut (<~1000 bars) and a WEIGHT,
//      not a gate mixer. BEHAVIOR: older high-quality analogs now qualify — expect
//      larger N with wider time coverage.
//  F2  Market-state vector expanded to 10 features: OB/FVG zone state added at a
//      fixed 8% weight (adaptive nine rescaled to 92).
//  F3  Per-direction hit probabilities from analog MFE/MAE distributions
//      (P[>=1R], P[>=2R], P[>=3R], P[SL 1R] for long and short, N>=20 gate).
//  F4  Trade plan shows P(TP1/TP2/TP3), P(SL), and 1R-expectancy (planReason);
//      NEGATIVE analog expectancy is a hard veto alongside TQ. TQ gains a
//      forecast-alignment component (weight 0.10) from that expectancy.
//  F5  Forecast analog weight scales with OOS effective sample (0.20 -> up to 0.30).
//  F6  Regime-transition tracking (6-state empirical matrix); persistence probability
//      shown next to the regime label ("S78%"). Regime-adaptive TQ minimum
//      (+15 ABNORMAL, +10 COMPRESS, -5 STRONG/EXPANSION), regime-conditioned TQ weights.
//  F7  Round-number (50s) levels join TP candidates; SL is nudged 0.2 ATR off exact
//      round numbers (stop-cluster avoidance).
// ═══════════════ Q5.1 additions ═══════════════
//  A  Scheduled-news windows (NFP first-Friday / CPI day 10-15, 12:15-14:00 UTC) now
//     trigger the ABNORMAL regime (confidence cap + size haircut) proactively.
//  B  Weekly + monthly anchored VWAPs (wVwapVal / mVwapVal).
//  C  VP POC / VAH / VAL and anchored VWAPs are first-class SL/TP candidates.
//  NOTE: VP levels are computed at the live edge; on historical bars they are na and
//  the plan falls back to the remaining candidates — deterministic, no repaint.
// ═══════════════ Q5.0 MASTER (quant-audit roadmap items implemented) ═══════════════
//  S1  Effective-N correction: overlapping OUTCOME_N-bar outcomes mean N_eff ~ N/OUTCOME_N.
//      Kelly's p is now the Wilson 95% LOWER bound at effective N (self-shrinking with
//      thin data); the OOS win-rate display carries a ± half-width at effective N.
//  S2  mP= is now Platt-FITTED: slope/intercept estimated by weighted least squares on
//      logit(realized frequency) vs mean bin score across calibration bins (>=3 bins of
//      >=30 samples, positive slope required); the heuristic slope remains the
//      cold-start fallback. "mapped, not fitted" (R5-F23) no longer applies once fit.
//  S3  Sharpe effective-N now uses the ESTIMATED lag-1 autocorrelation of the
//      chronological match-return series (fallback 0.3), clamped [0, 0.8].
//  S4  OOS embargo: records within OUTCOME_N bars of the IS/OOS boundary are excluded
//      from the OOS fold (outcome windows straddled both folds).
//  S5  London killzones are now EU-DST-aware (reuses the existing EU DST tracker);
//      session classification retains the documented fixed-hour simplification.
//  S6  Winsorization is timeframe-scaled (±6 sigma of raw returns, prev-bar window,
//      hard-bounded ±5%) — the fixed ±5% clamp was ~50 sigma on 5M bars (inactive).
//  S7  Cornish-Fisher inputs clamped to the expansion's monotone region (skew ±1,
//      excess kurtosis [-1, 3]); the existing hard fallback gate is retained.
//  S8  ADX gate hysteresis for BOS validity: ON above threshold, OFF below
//      threshold-2 — removes discontinuous signal flip-flop at the boundary.
//  Deferred (documented): empirical TQ/evidence re-weighting from the per-factor
//  conditional accumulators (medium complexity, overfit risk — needs live data first).
// ═══════════════ Q4.0-R6.0 EVOLUTION (on the R5.3 correctness base) ═══════════════
// Decision-support system for MANUAL MT5 execution. All R5.x validated logic preserved;
// R6.0 adds adaptive layers on top. Changed assumptions are documented at each site.
//  E1  ADAPTIVE MARKET REGIME ENGINE — every bar classified (ABNORMAL / COMPRESS /
//      EXPANSION / STRONG TR / WEAK TR / RANGE + HV/LV/NV volatility tag) using
//      percentile-based self-adapting thresholds (BB-width pct, ADX pct, ATR pct,
//      return z-score). Regime modulates: SL sizing (regSLMult 1.0-2.2), BOS volume
//      requirement (regBOSMult), liquidity proximity window (regLiqMult), forecast
//      cone horizon (regHorizonMult -> effForecastBars), size guidance (regSizeMult),
//      and caps displayed confidence at 60 in ABNORMAL (news-like) conditions.
//  E2  DYNAMIC TRADE PLAN — SL now selects the nearest valid STRUCTURAL level
//      (swing / order block / current-day extreme / PDL-PDH / equal highs-lows) on the
//      protective side, buffered 0.15 ATR, accepted within [0.6 ATR, 1.6 x regime-ATR];
//      regime-scaled ATR is only the fallback. TP1-TP3 target the nearest ranked
//      liquidity destinations (PDH/PWH/PMH/EQH/OB/CDH or mirror), deduped within
//      0.3 ATR, min 0.8R away; R-multiples only when the map is sparse. TP3 + all RRs
//      shown; the plan panel explains its own construction (planReason).
//  E3  TRADE QUALITY SCORE (0-100) — direction-conditioned, dynamically weighted
//      (trend/structure/liquidity/zone/macro-MTF/session/regime/analog/timing; analog
//      weight scales with OOS sample size; absent engines drop out of the weight sum).
//      Below tqMinScore (input, default 55): decision shows NO TRADE and alerts are
//      suppressed. Displayed as TQ<score><grade> in the decision box.
//  E4  SESSION INTELLIGENCE — per-session (Asian/London/NY) EWMA average range,
//      live expansion % vs that average, historical manipulation frequency (prior
//      session's extreme swept then rejected), and directional-continuation frequency.
//      Shown in the session cell as Exp/M/C once >= 5 sessions of data exist.
//  E5  EXPLAINABILITY — decisionLog (R5.1) + planReason (SL basis, TP bases, regime)
//      + regime cell + TQ grade give a full why-chain for every recommendation.
// Assumption changes vs R5.3: SL is no longer fixed 1.5 ATR (structural, regime-scaled
// fallback); TP ladder is liquidity-first instead of fixed 1R/2R; BOS volume gate and
// liquidity proximity flex with volatility percentile; forecast cone shortens in
// compression/abnormal and lengthens in expansion/strong trend.
// Q4.0-R5.3 fixes (remaining items from the end-to-end audit):
//  M1  MaxDD basis: equity is now a notional %-account starting at 100, each match
//      contributing riskPercent x |ATR move| / 1.5 (the plan's 1.5-ATR risk unit).
//      MaxDD% is now a real account-drawdown estimate on the same scale as maxDdPct,
//      so the useDDBreaker gate and Kelly haircuts act on a meaningful number.
//      (Previous curve started at 0 in raw ATR units — %-of-peak was scale-arbitrary.)
//  M2  Analog similarity: cosine on non-negative features (~0.95-1.0 for any pair,
//      i.e. matching was really just recency decay) replaced with 1 - weighted mean
//      |difference|. Identical states = 1.0; discrimination is now per-feature.
//      Expect LOWER oMatch/N than R5.2 — retune histW* / observe _simThresh if needed.
//  M3  Calibration target: hPred/hCalBin slot is overwritten after the blend+forecast
//      pipeline with the FINAL displayed bullScore, so Cal grade / Brier / mP= now
//      validate the number actually shown (mildly self-referential via the 70/30
//      blend — accepted trade-off, documented at the write site).
//  M6  History scan iterates the ring buffer in chronological order (oldest = slot hW
//      when full); equity/MaxDD accumulate inline; per-chunk sort stage removed.
//      Also: MaxDD stored before Calmar (was dividing by the previous cycle's DD).
//  --  Forecast double-history: oBosCont term removed from fAdj (same historical DB
//      was already blended into bullScore — history entered twice).
//  --  OUTCOME_N floor 1 -> 3: >=1H charts no longer collapse to next-bar drift, and
//      the PDH/PDL first-touch loop is no longer degenerate at N=1.
//  L3  MAE forward-window off-by-one fixed; historical ATR lookback cap 2000 -> 4999.
//  L4  HTF mid EMA 50 -> 100 — all trend engines now share the 20/100/200 definition.
//      NOTE: shifts HTF bull/bear gates vs R5.2 (slower regime flips).
//  L5  Structure persistence = bars since BOS while the BOS-origin protective level
//      holds (was: only bars making simultaneous new HH+HL, which never accumulated).
//  L6  liqHealth "staleness" check removed (it penalized successful liquidity runs);
//      budget folded into availability tiers.
//  L8  tc()/tcb() parameter no longer shadows the function name.
//  L7  accepted as-is (documented at the HTF availability block).
// BEHAVIOR NOTE: M1/M2/M3/L4/L5 all change dashboard statistics and gates vs R5.2.
// Re-record expected values and re-observe signal frequency before trusting
// useDDBreaker or Kelly output on live charts.
// Q4.0-R5.2 fixes (external end-to-end audit):
//  C1  crossedNYWeek checked the crossing bar's own UTC day for Friday — impossible on
//      XAUUSD (the weekly boundary is crossed by the Sunday open bar). PWH/PWL never
//      rolled: prev-weekly levels were stuck at first-bar values, contaminating weekly
//      liquidity pools, sweeps, destination ranking, liqHealth, and key-level lines.
//      Now tests dayofweek(time[1]) == Friday.
//  C2  FVG engine: bearish gap bounds were the full 3-bar envelope (now [high[0],low[2]]);
//      fvgWasBullish was set on the bearish condition (now low[0] > high[2]); the swapped
//      mitigation tests were trivially true, so every FVG self-mitigated within a bar
//      (now requires a later bar to trade strictly into the gap interior). Display lines
//      un-swapped. fvgActiveCount no longer leaks on fvgMaxBars expiry.
//  H1  tInv sign inversion made all correlation significance thresholds negative,
//      forcing corrWinScore onto its rs*10 fallback — the R5-F9 t-dist/Bonferroni
//      machinery was dead code. NOTE: corr-health values will drop materially now that
//      real significance thresholds apply.
//  H2  evCorrBear treated correlation breakdown as bearish evidence (latent short bias
//      during decoupling rallies). Corr stream is now direction-neutral; breakdown
//      feeds rangeEvidence (+10) instead.
//  M4  mtfConfluenceScore denominator 9 -> 10 (max votes = 4 MTF + 6 macro).
//  M5  Cone breach state moved to main scope (was dashboard-only) and its degenerate
//      test fixed (close > close + band could never be true). Breach = 1-bar move
//      beyond Z*ATR from the prior bar's cone origin.
//  L1  confLabel abbreviation comparisons used wrong case (dead branches).
//  L2  Forecast-reached "✓" label is now a managed singleton (was leaking labels).
// Known open items after R5.3 (design-level, intentional): L7 unconditional lower-TF
// security calls (documented in place); session-hour simplifications (London open fixed
// 07:00 UTC, Asian = 00-07 UTC); Asian "range" is a rolling 7h high/low; Kelly p is
// state-conditioned 1h-drift rate, not trade-structure win rate (haircuts compensate).
// NOTE: Expected values below were recorded while the historical analog engine was
// disabled by the similarity-scale bug (fixed in R5). R5.2 additionally changes PWH/PWL,
// correlation health, evidence scores, and confidence on every bar — re-record after this build:
// (5M chart, 2026-06-23): close=4126, ADX=28, DXY=104.2 → bullScore/bearScore/rangeScore STALE
// Input bounds: adxThreshold [10,50], forecastBars [5,30],
// internalPivotLen [1,5], swingPivotLen [3,10]
// Q4.0-R5 external audit fixes:
//  F1  similarity threshold scale (sim*100 vs 35-65) — analog engine now actually matches
//  F2  removed undefined regimeBull/regimeBear from DoW tracker
//  F3  removed invalid ta.dayofweek (reuses global _dow)
//  F4  _ddForBreaker persistent mirror fixes oMaxDD use-before-declaration + same-bar loop
//  F5  hline(series) replaced with plot()
//  F6  dead EWMA vol block deleted (wrong half-life claim, never consumed)
//  F7  per-hour volume average: warm-up then EWMA (was unbounded all-history mean)
//  F8  S/R strengths now rebuilt per scan and incremented on cluster touches
//  F9  Bonferroni corrected for 18 tests (6 assets x 3 windows)
//  F10 session bias made direction-neutral
//  F11 cone label shows Z multiple, not a bogus coverage %
//  F12 alertcondition messages use only valid built-in placeholders
//  F13 DXY/10Y dashboard arrows now show impact on gold (per legend)
//  F14 textSize "Medium" no longer produces an invalid size constant
//  F15 round-trip cost = spread + 2x slippage (spread was double-counted)
//  F16 crossedNYDay midnight-wrap now checks both sides of the boundary
//  F17 displacement hysteresis simplified (dead exit branch removed)
//  F18 EQH/EQL label tolerance unified on eqAtrMult input
//  F19 stationarity guard wired into confidenceScore
//  F20 regimeScore clamped at 100
//  F21 empty news-session string guarded
//  F22 liq hierarchy check removed (penalized normal early-week states)
//  F23 "P=" renamed "mP=" — mapped, not fitted, probability
// Q4.0-R5.1 traceability pass (F24): every computed value now has a consumer.
//  Wired: QVERSION/_symStr/_tfLabel→footer; _coneStatus+_csLabel→RISK row2; avgCorrSPX→adaptive wSPX;
//  ratePressure (yield ROC) + EURUSD ROC→macro momentum msRate; vwapSlope/vwapAccel→VWAP scenarios;
//  vwapRejectBull/Bear→aligned-signal counters; climaxUp/Down→plotshape markers; cvdBull/Bear+vdK+
//  session vol EWMA→MARKET row2; mtfAgreementHigh/Med + _htfBias→BIAS row2; calProbStr→SIGNAL row2;
//  _structActiveBg/_macroBg/_macro2Col/_volCol/_biasCol→cell colors; per-target reach scores→TGT suffix;
//  oPdh1stPct/oPdl1stPct→Brk line; oBosFail+oCalDetail→advanced FUT line; oMaxAdverseATR→risk row3;
//  wrCIStr→risk row2; liqHealthScore→liquidity row3; vpocPrice/vaPos/vaRatio→PRICE row3;
//  obBull/BearVolPct→OB labels; fvgVolPctAtDetect→FVG label; tpDirStr/tpCol/tp*Str/tpRRStr→plan panel;
//  debugMode→DECISION debug line; density→table width scaling.
//  Removed (pure leftovers, no coherent consumer): unused palette constants, macro1..5Color,
//  dxyC/yldC/eurC/slvC, _stateCol/_qualCol/_mtfCol/_tfArrows/_nearAboveCol/_nearBelowCol/_rrCol/_prVal,
//  cvdMA50, volRatio, obBull/BearAtr, fvgAtrAtDetect, _csEnd/_csEndBand/_fcCurr/_csSlope,
//  absFr/_absFrSorted, local _eStr/_slStr/_tpStr (superseded by global tp*Str).

// INSTITUTIONAL COLOR PALETTE — 5-color standard
// Bull: #00D084 | Bear: #FF4D4D | Neutral: #A0A0A0
// Liq: #00C2FF | Warn: #FF8C00

// Division safety helper — prevents NaN from 0 denominator
// I7 (§16 harness): the guard tested `b != 0`, which a denominator of 1e-12 passes --
// safeDiv(10, 1e-12) returned ~1e13. §3(E) asks whether any denominator can go zero,
// near-zero or regime-dependent; this covered only the exact-zero case. A relative
// epsilon closes the near-zero case too. NUMERICAL STABILITY, not a behavioural change:
// the only results it alters are ones that were already numerically meaningless.
safeDiv(a, b) => not na(a) and not na(b) and math.abs(b) > 1e-10 ? a / b : 0.0

// Bayesian-smoothed win rate: (wins + 1) / (total + 2), uniform Beta(1,1) prior
// Pulls small-sample bin rates toward 50%, preventing overfitting on <30 samples
bayesRate(w, t) => t > 0 ? (w + 1) / (t + 2) : 0.5

// S/R level scanner: fractal + volume-weighted clustering (runs once per confirmed last bar)
// R5-F8: arrays are rebuilt on every scan and cluster re-touches increment the level's
// strength, so srStrengths now genuinely counts fractal touches inside the scan window
// (previously strengths were pushed as 1.0 and never incremented — tiers were dead).
// AUDIT FIX (R4): separate arrays per side, each with an independent cap, so a support
// slot can never silently hold a resistance level.
// Bloomberg Terminal palette (dashboard only — chart visuals unchanged)
color cBloomBull = color.new(#00C853, 0)
color cBloomBear = color.new(#FF5252, 0)
color cBloomWarn = color.new(#FFC107, 0)
color cBloomNeut = color.new(#9E9E9E, 0)
// Extended color system for visual hierarchy
color C_TEXT = color.white

// MODULE TOGGLES (reduced)
grpModules = "MODULES"
perfMode = input.bool(false, "Institutional Performance Mode", group=grpModules)
showFVG = input.bool(false, "Fair Value Gaps", group=grpModules, tooltip="Legacy in-Master drawing, OFF by default. The Visuals companion draws this. Turn this ON only if running the Master ALONE — with both scripts loaded you get two overlapping sets, and the S/R algorithms differ (Master: pivot-strength scan; companion: ATR-clustered touch counts), so the two will disagree on level prices.")
showOB = input.bool(false, "Order Blocks", group=grpModules, tooltip="Legacy in-Master drawing, OFF by default. The Visuals companion draws this. Turn this ON only if running the Master ALONE — with both scripts loaded you get two overlapping sets, and the S/R algorithms differ (Master: pivot-strength scan; companion: ATR-clustered touch counts), so the two will disagree on level prices.")
showSMT = input.bool(false, "SMT Divergence", group=grpModules)
showClimax = input.bool(false, "Volume Climax", group=grpModules)
showAdaptiveATR = input.bool(false, "Adaptive ATR Regime", group=grpModules)
showDisplacement = input.bool(false, "Displacement Candles", group=grpModules)
showForecastCone = input.bool(false, "Forecast Cone", group=grpModules)
